WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.239 --> 00:00:03.669
-Republicans are trying
to rile up their base

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:06.305
in response to President Biden's
new vaccine requirements.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:09.808
And Rudy Giuliani insisted
he was not drunk

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:12.278
when he went on a bizarre rant
during a speech

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.913
at a 9/11 memorial dinner.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.315
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:20.053
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.654
The modern Republican Party

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.190
is a bizarre
and unhinged institution

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:28.060
populated by crime-adjacent
weirdos who pander nonstop

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.463
to the ugliest instincts
of their base to stay relevant.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.065
For example, Republicans
have spent the last few days

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.935
expressing outrage
not over the deadly virus

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.304
that's killed
more than 650,000 Americans

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.873
and is currently
overwhelming hospitals

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.607
and ICUs across the country,

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.275
but about
the president's attempt

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:46.279
to get people vaccinated
against that virus.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.748
-There are a number
of Republican governors

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.350
who have vowed
to fight this order.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.352
Texas Governor Greg Abbott
tweeted, "Texas

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:56.255
is already working to halt
this power grab."

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:58.424
-Governor Brian Kemp of Georgia
posting

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.727
he will pursue
every legal option

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.996
"to stop this blatantly
unlawful overreach

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.765
by the Biden administration."

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.333
-South Dakota Governor
Kristi Noem

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:10.102
tweeting at Joe Biden,
"See you in court."

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.104
-One of the most heinous
displays

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.006
we've ever seen
from a president.

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:16.809
-He is the closest thing
we've gotten to a dictator yet.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.278
-J.D. Vance, Republican
candidate for Senate in Ohio,

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:21.847
released a statement urging
people to ignore the president.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:23.616
"Do not comply
with the mandates,"

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.184
which, just to be clear,
he's saying,

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:26.819
"Don't get vaccinated."

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:29.088
"Only mass civil disobedience
will save us

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.257
from Joe Biden's
naked authoritarianism."

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.260
-The governor of South Carolina,
Henry McMaster, tweeting,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.963
"Rest assured, we will fight
them to the gates of hell

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.898
to protect the liberty
and livelihood

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.299
of every South Carolinian."

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.067
-Take it easy, Henry.
You're not even gonna fight

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.836
somebody to the gates
of your community.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:47.673
And I'm sorry, you'll fight them
to the gates of hell?

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:49.942
It's a requirement
to get vaccinated

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.977
against a deadly
respiratory virus,

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:53.979
and you sound like
you're writing a screenplay

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:56.315
for a direct-to-VHS
Steven Seagal movie

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:57.784
called "Strike Force One."

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.253
"The Russians have boarded
the boat, and they have nukes!"

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.288
[ As Seagal ] "We'll fight them
to the gates of hell.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.723
Now, get me my nunchucks."

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.124
[ Normal voice ] Nunchucks?!
Didn't you hear me?

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.525
They have nukes!"

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:09.695
[ As Seagal ] "Don't worry.
I'll hide behind that pipe."

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.731
[ Normal voice ] But that's
what these people do.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.066
It's all performance
and manufactured outrage,

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:15.568
designed to gin up their base.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.638
They don't seem to care about
the toll of the virus itself

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.406
and the immense loss and grief
it's wrought.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.442
They just care
about mimicking Trump

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:25.044
to pander to their voters.
That's why guys like J.D. Vance,

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.846
who once called
Trump reprehensible,

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.781
are now calling
for mass civil disobedience

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.349
and telling GOP primary voters,

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.285
"Do not comply,"
which I don't get.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.953
It's one thing to say,
"I'm pro-vaccine,

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.788
but against mandates,"
but these guys are acting

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.923
like mandates are tyranny,
when in reality,

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:41.026
mandates exist everywhere
and we have to do all kinds

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:42.494
of much more annoying things
every day

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:44.597
to live in a functioning society
with other people.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.399
I mean, do you think anyone
likes waiting in line at the DMV

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:48.901
in order to be able
to commute to work?

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.004
No one likes that,
but we do it.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.439
I was at the DMV
for a full day one time

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.275
because I waited in line
to change my address.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.678
And when I got to the booth,
I forgot my pen.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.612
So they told me to wait
in the pen line,

00:03:00.612 --> 00:03:01.880
which took another three hours.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.716
When I got to the window
for a pen,

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:04.984
they told me how
to fill out a form.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.452
And I said, "But
I don't have a pen."

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.721
And they said,
"That's not my problem."

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.224
But we all have to do
[Bleep] like that.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.625
And it's not just
a personal choice.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.228
I can't believe I still
have to say this, 18 months in.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.563
But you can spread COVID
to other people.

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:19.765
It's not just about yourself.
That's the difference.

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:22.635
And the Republicans calling
Biden a tyrant or dictator

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.470
for implementing
workplace safety rules,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.807
which multiple polls have now
shown have majority support,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.442
did you have the same reaction

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:32.111
when Trump claimed he had
the unilateral authority

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.613
to order every governor
in the country

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.915
to reopen their states
and force everyone back to work

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.450
before a vaccine even existed?

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.819
-There's a debate
over what authority you have

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:43.489
to order the country reopened.
What authority do you have?

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.957
-Well, I have
the ultimate authority.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:47.293
The president of the
United States has the authority

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.496
to do what the president
has the authority to do,

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.864
which is very powerful.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:55.034
When somebody is the president
of the United States,

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:58.270
the authority is total, and
that's the way it's got to be.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.473
I have the absolute right
to do it if I want to.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:04.076
-Again, the ultimate authority
sounds like a direct-to-VHS

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:06.312
Steven Seagal movie,
where he plays an ex-Navy SEAL

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.846
who works at a mall
when it gets taken over

00:04:07.846 --> 00:04:09.081
by Russian terrorists.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.415
[ As Seagal ]
"I'm in charge here.

00:04:10.415 --> 00:04:13.552
I have the ultimate authority.
Now get me my katana.

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.187
It's the, um --

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.256
it's, like, the
Japanese sword-looking thing."

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.125
[ Normal voice ] And
for those of you asking,

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.694
"Why is it okay for Biden
but not Trump,

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.662
there's a moral
and legal difference

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.464
between claiming the power

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:27.634
to implement
new workplace safety rules

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.536
and claiming total authority
to force everyone back to work

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.405
to expose themselves
to a deadly virus.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:35.074
If you're comparing the two,
you're doing so in bad faith.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.042
That's like saying
there's no difference

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:38.945
between forcing people
to wear a seatbelt

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:42.481
and forcing car manufacturers
to install a third mystery pedal

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.817
on the driver's side that
either brakes, accelerates,

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:48.921
or launches you straight up into
the sky without a parachute.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.890
And as for Biden,
he's not backing down,

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.458
even in the face
of GOP hysterics,

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:53.960
as he made clear
over the weekend.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.702
-Have at it.

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:06.672
-Damn, a lot of Seagal energy
going around these days!

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:08.674
"Gates of hell," "Have at it."

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:11.343
Politicians are starting to talk
like one of those movies

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:13.512
about two old boxers
who come out of retirement

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.515
to settle a feud one more time.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.149
"I'll send you
to the gates of hell."

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:18.751
"Have at it!"
"What?"

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:21.120
"I said, 'Have at it.'"
"Have at what?"

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.723
The GOP has been like this
for decades,

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.458
but the party's
latest transformation

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.759
into whatever it is now

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:30.129
is perhaps best embodied
by former Mayor Rudy Giuliani,

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:32.231
who the media once hailed
as America's mayor,

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.733
but who is now essentially
a New York City Bigfoot

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:36.836
who hangs out with
Eastern European mobsters

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.605
and trims his toenails
in Panera bathrooms.

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.507
I don't even know
if he's really done that,

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.310
but, I mean, would you be
surprised at this point?

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.845
I wouldn't be surprised
if I was watching

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.580
an episode of
"World's Dumbest Criminals"

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.115
and I saw Rudy
on a Duane Reade security camera

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:51.783
trying to use his own keys

00:05:51.783 --> 00:05:55.154
to open the shelf
where they keep all the razors.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.689
I wouldn't even be surprised

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.158
if an employee walked over
and said, "You again?!"

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:02.728
In 2001, he was front row
at Yankees playoff games,

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:05.498
and now I'm pretty sure
he sells off-brand merchandise

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.466
on the sidewalk
outside the stadium.

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:08.567
[ As Giuliani ]
"It doesn't say 'N.Y.'

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:11.003
It says 'M.Y.'
for 'my Yankees.'"

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.471
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:13.840
[ Normal voice ]
And then, on Saturday night,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.741
during an appearance
at what has traditionally

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:19.478
been a somber event,
an annual 9/11 memorial dinner,

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:21.647
Rudy went on an incoherent rant

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:24.417
where he, among other things,
imitated Queen Elizabeth

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.285
and insisted out of nowhere

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.788
that he never spent any time
with Prince Andrew.

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:32.491
-Rudy Giuliani does
an annual dinner every year

00:06:32.491 --> 00:06:33.960
with people
who were involved with him

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.462
on September 11, 2001,
and for years.

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:39.398
you know, my impression was,
it was a somber,

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:43.503
poignant gathering of people
to talk about what was lost

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:47.740
and how the city
saw itself through that time.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.208
Not really anymore.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.210
-I don't want to sound
like a name-dropper,

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.246
but I showed this
to the Queen of England.

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:57.149
She said, [As Queen Elizabeth]
"You did a wonderful job

00:06:57.149 --> 00:07:01.687
on September 11,
and therefore, I'm making you

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:06.024
an honorary knight,
commander of the royal

00:07:06.024 --> 00:07:07.693
[Normal voice]
something or other."

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:09.962
[ Laughter ]
I turned down a knighthood

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.129
because if you took
a knighthood,

00:07:11.129 --> 00:07:13.299
you had to lose
your citizenship.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:16.302
I know Prince Andrew
is very questionable now.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:19.105
I never went out with him.
Never.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:21.707
Never -- Never
had a drink with him.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:24.710
Never was with a woman
or a young girl with him,

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.779
ever, ever, ever.
One time,

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:28.180
I met him in my office,

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.782
and one time
when we had the party.

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:31.583
Right, Bernie? You were there.

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:33.853
-What a time to be Bernie.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:35.988
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:37.789
I'm assuming that's
Bernie Kerik.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:40.158
But I don't know,
and Rudy probably doesn't know.

00:07:40.158 --> 00:07:41.460
Bernie was probably
right in the middle

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.095
of bragging
about his great seats,

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:46.164
and then Rudy bails on his act
to do some crowd work.

00:07:46.164 --> 00:07:47.767
[ As Giuliani ] "Right, Bernie?
We had that podium.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:50.035
Prince Andrew was there,
and nothing creepy happened.

00:07:50.035 --> 00:07:52.805
That was right before
you got indicted, right, Bernie?

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:54.239
Give it up for Bernie,
everybody.

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:56.442
He was with me
when we met Prince Andrew.

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:58.311
Nothin' happened!"

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.945
You were there
and I were there

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:02.881
and Prince Andrew was there,
but it was normal."

00:08:02.881 --> 00:08:06.652
[ Normal voice ] Look, I'm
not saying Rudy was drunk,

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:08.987
but that's usually
when guys from Brooklyn

00:08:08.987 --> 00:08:11.356
start trying to imitate
the Queen of England.

00:08:11.356 --> 00:08:13.792
If you're ever in a Coney Island
dive bar at 3:00 a.m.,

00:08:13.792 --> 00:08:15.227
and someone orders
and Amstel Light

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:16.595
instead of a Budweiser,

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:18.697
you can expect to hear
one of his friends say,

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:20.198
"Look at this [Bleep] guy.

00:08:20.198 --> 00:08:22.768
Oh, I'll have the Amstel Light,
and I'm the Queen of England."

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.136
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.338
But I guess, now that
we've heard his British accent,

00:08:26.338 --> 00:08:29.141
we know why Rudy lost out
on the part of Mrs. Doubtfire.

00:08:29.141 --> 00:08:31.644
Of course, if he ever tried
to Doubtfire his ex-wife,

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:33.245
she would figure it out
right away.

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:35.347
[British accent] "Would you like
a spot of tea, dear?"

00:08:35.347 --> 00:08:36.715
[ Normal voice ]
I know it's you, Rudy.

00:08:36.715 --> 00:08:38.684
You're my cousin.

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:41.954
But I guess Rudy
can add this tape

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:43.289
to his reel of impressions

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:46.124
if he ever auditions
for "America's Not Talent."

00:08:46.124 --> 00:08:47.659
-One time, Bill Clinton
asked me,

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:50.362
"What's this guy Romney like?"
You know what I told him?

00:08:50.362 --> 00:08:53.565
"He's our Al Gore."

00:08:53.565 --> 00:08:56.469
-Alright, Rudy.
-"I'm Spartacus."

00:08:56.469 --> 00:09:00.205
Mueller's saying,
"Obstruction of justice."

00:09:00.205 --> 00:09:02.875
"Obstruction of justice."
Which the guy will say,

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:05.644
"Say 'obstruction of justice.'"
"Obstruction of justice."

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:08.547
"Did you decide it?"
"No."

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:11.016
-Well, I'm definitely not going
to Rudy's one-man show.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:12.518
I'm just kidding.
I definitely am.

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:15.521
Why do all of Rudy's impressions
sound like a cartoon dog?

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:17.523
He sounds like McGruff
the Crime Dog

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:21.660
blitzed out of his mind on some
cocaine confiscated from a bust.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.230
And by the way, for the record,

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.766
Rudy would like everyone to know
he was definitely not drunk.

00:09:27.766 --> 00:09:29.035
And he let everyone know
in a way

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:31.370
that's very uncharacteristic
of drunk guys.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.405
He gave a series of long,
rambling answers

00:09:33.405 --> 00:09:35.241
in which he repeated himself
and made no sense.

00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:37.009
Rudy gave an interview
over the weekend,

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:40.446
and I'm going to read it to you,
the actual transcript,

00:09:40.446 --> 00:09:43.616
like a guy trying to get
his keys from the bartender.

00:09:43.616 --> 00:09:46.118
"Yes, I had a scotch,
but I was not drunk.

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:48.654
There is a deliberate attempt
by the left wing

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:51.257
to paint me that way."
"I'm not a drunk.

00:09:51.257 --> 00:09:54.092
I don't think I've ever been
publicly drunk in my life.

00:09:54.092 --> 00:09:56.529
The last time I was --
I was probably in college."

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:58.998
"I like to drink Scotch
and have cigars.

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:00.098
That's where it probably
comes from.

00:10:00.098 --> 00:10:03.502
I drink moderate amounts
of Scotch.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:05.737
I mostly drink Scotch because
I like to have it with cigars."

00:10:05.737 --> 00:10:07.273
"I didn't have a cigar
last night.

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:10.676
And this is a caricature that
the left is trying to put on me.

00:10:10.676 --> 00:10:12.678
I can't remember the last time
that I was drunk."

00:10:12.678 --> 00:10:14.179
"Yes, of course I had a Scotch
at the beginning of dinner,

00:10:14.179 --> 00:10:17.049
Beyond that, I didn't have --
it was watered down."

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:18.918
"Not even sure I drank
the whole thing."

00:10:18.918 --> 00:10:21.754
"It hurts my reputation for
someone to say I'm drunk."

00:10:21.754 --> 00:10:23.088
I'm not sure I agree, though.

00:10:23.088 --> 00:10:24.290
It's probably better
if you were drunk.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.725
At least your behavior
would make sense.

00:10:25.725 --> 00:10:27.393
If someone told you,
"Hey, so, last night,

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:29.895
Dave gets up in karaoke
and instead of singing,

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:32.999
he just listed everything
he hated about each of us

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:34.833
while Duran Duran
played in the background.

00:10:34.833 --> 00:10:36.635
Then, he stormed out
with his pants down,

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:39.204
and then later, when we left,
he was asleep in a bush.

00:10:39.204 --> 00:10:40.505
Craziest thing was,
didn't have a drink.

00:10:40.505 --> 00:10:42.341
Just like that."
If you heard that,

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:43.976
you'd say, "Well,
I think it's probably

00:10:43.976 --> 00:10:46.211
the end of our time
hanging out with Dave."

00:10:46.211 --> 00:10:48.347
But, sure, that's what's
hurting your reputation.

00:10:48.347 --> 00:10:50.382
Not the fact you helped
incite a riot at the Capitol,

00:10:50.382 --> 00:10:52.684
lied about the election,
had your law license suspended,

00:10:52.684 --> 00:10:54.019
forgot to swing
your balls forward

00:10:54.019 --> 00:10:55.388
before you sat down
for an interview,

00:10:55.388 --> 00:10:56.822
accidentally
gave a press conference

00:10:56.822 --> 00:10:58.156
outside a landscape company,

00:10:58.156 --> 00:10:59.825
had hair dye leaking out
of the side of your head

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:01.727
like the juice
leaking from a Hefty bag,

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:06.798
and got caught shaving
at a table in an airport.

00:11:06.798 --> 00:11:08.167
Can you imagine
being his waiter?

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:09.535
"What can I get for you, sir?"

00:11:09.535 --> 00:11:11.903
"Uh, I'll have some tap water
and a can of Barbasol."

00:11:11.903 --> 00:11:13.906
So, Rudy insists
he wasn't drunk,

00:11:13.906 --> 00:11:16.975
but he does like to engage
in doing English accents.

00:11:16.975 --> 00:11:19.411
Giuliani said the idea that he
was mocking the Queen

00:11:19.411 --> 00:11:21.780
is "an interpretation
that's totally unfair.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.516
I used an English accent."
"And I have never mocked it.

00:11:24.516 --> 00:11:27.920
I just like to use an English --
I imitate Churchill sometimes."

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.422
The only thing
you have in common

00:11:29.422 --> 00:11:31.223
with Churchill
is a stiff upper lip,

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:33.892
and that's just
early-onset rigor mortis.

00:11:33.892 --> 00:11:35.827
So, Rudy thinks he's
just like Churchill.

00:11:35.827 --> 00:11:37.796
Of course, if you told Rudy
to wear a Homburg hat,

00:11:37.796 --> 00:11:40.366
he'd probably show up
with a Big Mac on his head.

00:11:40.366 --> 00:11:42.067
[ Laughter ]

00:11:42.067 --> 00:11:44.537
This is the modern GOP --
rambling, incoherent,

00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:46.238
and far more outraged
about attempts

00:11:46.238 --> 00:11:47.807
to stop a deadly virus
from spreading

00:11:47.807 --> 00:11:50.342
than the toll
that the deadly virus has taken,

00:11:50.342 --> 00:11:52.043
and that's because Trumpism
is still the core

00:11:52.043 --> 00:11:54.146
of the modern GOP.
Trump led one of the most

00:11:54.146 --> 00:11:55.781
disastrous presidencies
in history,

00:11:55.781 --> 00:11:57.483
and all Republicans have
to say about him is...

00:11:57.483 --> 00:11:59.351
-[As Queen Elizabeth]
"You did a wonderful job."

00:11:59.351 --> 00:12:01.486
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:01.486 --> 00:12:04.990
[ Theme music plays ]

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.491
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:12:06.491 --> 00:12:08.627
over 2 million meals a year
to men, women, and children

00:12:08.627 --> 00:12:11.563
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:12:11.563 --> 00:12:13.064
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:12:13.064 --> 00:12:15.033
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:12:15.033 --> 00:12:17.403
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

